{
  "name": "FrameFocus Dev",
  "image": "mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/typescript-node:20",
  "postCreateCommand": "npm install",
  "forwardPorts": [3000, 8081],
  // ⚠️ PORT 3000 DEFAULTS TO **PRIVATE** ON REBUILD, AND IS DELIBERATELY MADE
  // PUBLIC BY HAND WHEN OAUTH IS BEING EXERCISED. TWO STATES, ON PURPOSE.
  // [Changed from a public default at S105b item 10, RULED Josh.]
  //
  // WHY PRIVATE IS THE DEFAULT. This dev server talks to rebuild-test, and a
  // PUBLIC forwarded port is reachable by anyone who has the URL. A public
  // default meant every rebuild silently came back internet-reachable — a state
  // nobody re-consented to. Private-on-rebuild makes exposure an explicit,
  // deliberate act rather than the resting state of a disposable box.
  //
  // WHY IT MUST BE MADE PUBLIC FOR OAUTH. Codespaces forwards ports PRIVATE by
  // default; a private port answers any request that does not carry a GitHub
  // tunnel cookie with a 302 to `https://github.dev/pf-signin?...` -- the request
  // never reaches the dev server, and nothing is logged, because nothing arrived.
  // That breaks the two 7G routes an outside party calls directly:
  //
  //   /api/quickbooks/callback  Intuit redirects the BROWSER here after
  //                             consent. It is a CROSS-SITE navigation from
  //                             appcenter.intuit.com, so the tunnel cookie is
  //                             not presented and the sign-in interstitial
  //                             swallows the `code`. The connection silently
  //                             never completes.
  //   /api/quickbooks/webhook   Intuit POSTs here with NO session, ever. It
  //                             would see 302s instead of 200s and, after
  //                             retries at 20/30/50 minutes, DISABLE THE
  //                             ENDPOINT.
  //
  // So item 1 (connecting a real company) STILL needs a public port -- but as an
  // explicit step, not a standing default.
  //
  // ⚠️ THIS IS A DEVELOPMENT CONCERN ONLY. Production is Vercel on its own
  // domain with no tunnel in front of it, and is unaffected.
  //
  // ⚠️ CHANGING THIS VALUE ONLY AFFECTS THE NEXT CREATE/REBUILD. An
  // ALREADY-RUNNING Codespace keeps whatever visibility it has, so making it
  // public for an OAuth session does NOT survive a rebuild (that is the point).
  // Flip the LIVE port in the VS Code PORTS panel (right-click 3000 -> Port
  // Visibility -> Public), or with `gh codespace ports visibility 3000:public`.
  "portsAttributes": {
    "3000": { "label": "Next.js Web", "onAutoForward": "notify", "visibility": "private" },
    "8081": { "label": "Expo Mobile", "onAutoForward": "notify" }
  },
  "customizations": {
    "vscode": {
      "settings": {
        "editor.defaultFormatter": "esbenp.prettier-vscode",
        "editor.formatOnSave": true,
        "editor.tabSize": 2,
        "typescript.tsdk": "node_modules/typescript/lib",
        "tailwindCSS.experimental.classRegex": [
          ["cva\\(([^)]*)\\)", "[\"'`]([^\"'`]*).*?[\"'`]"]
        ]
      },
      "extensions": [
        "dbaeumer.vscode-eslint",
        "esbenp.prettier-vscode",
        "bradlc.vscode-tailwindcss",
        "formulahendry.auto-rename-tag",
        "ms-azuretools.vscode-docker"
      ]
    }
  }
}
